###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - MACE and ANI-2x errors on the COMP6 subsets are measured against different references (B3LYP-D3BJ/def2-SV(P) recomputed here for MACE; the omegaB97x/6-31G(d) COMP6 values for ANI-2x), as the authors state; the two are not errors against the same ground truth. The reference calculation of this file is the B3LYP one.
# - Energy RMSEs are in kcal/mol per atom (no unit individual; mlips:hasUnit omitted).
# - MACE hyperparameters are in Table S1 of the Supporting Information, not in the PDF read; no setting is encoded.
# - The paper's headline results, bond dissociation energies (RMSE 1.37 kcal/mol on CYP 3A4 substrates) and their rank correlation against DFT, AM1, GFN2-xTB and ALFABET, and geometry RMSDs (Table 3), have no MetricProperty.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
